WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.800
Let’s walk through Your role in the exercise.

00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:07.025
Use this opening step to establish ownership before learning controls

00:00:07.025 --> 00:00:07.200
.

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:10.287
Identify what this seat creates or reviews, what must

00:00:10.287 --> 00:00:13.400
be handed to another role, and which decisions remain

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:15.113
outside your authority.

00:00:15.113 --> 00:00:17.738
On this slide, as White Cell Support, you

00:00:17.738 --> 00:00:22.275
operate the control-cell boundary across timing, review, information

00:00:22.275 --> 00:00:23.863
, and session evidence.

00:00:24.410 --> 00:00:28.260
In practice, keep deterministic exercise state in the platform

00:00:28.260 --> 00:00:31.035
, make every review outcome explicit, and leave a

00:00:31.035 --> 00:00:34.347
chronological record another operator can audit.

00:00:34.347 --> 00:00:37.185
Before you continue, verify these points:

00:00:37.185 --> 00:00:40.610
The Lead owns privileged run and review decisions.

00:00:40.610 --> 00:00:44.297
Support follows the permissions actually exposed to that seat.

00:00:44.297 --> 00:00:48.435
Participant visibility never substitutes for White Cell review.
